{{also|scheissen|schéissen}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|de|scheissen||Switzerland|Liechtenstein}}
* {{alt|de|sch**ßen|sch**ssen||censored}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|schīzen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|*skīzan}} (attested as {{m|goh|biskīzan}}), from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*skītaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*skeyd-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*sḱeyd-||to part with, separate, cut off}}. Compare {{cog|nds|schieten}}, {{cog|nl|schijten}}, and {{cog|en|shit#Verb|shit}}, Danish {{m|da|skide}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃaɪ̯sn̩/|/ˈʃaɪ̯sən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-scheißen.ogg}}
* {{hyph|de|schei|ßen}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|scheißen<schiss,geschissen>}}

# {{lb|de|vulgar}} to [[shit]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''scheiß'''' mir gleich in die Hose!|t=I'm about to '''shit''' my trousers!}}
# {{lb|de|vulgar}} to be [[uninterested]] in; to [[ignore]]; to not [[give a shit]] about {{+obj|de|:auf(acc)<someone/something>}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''scheiße''' auf diese Regeln.|t=I don't '''give a shit''' about these rules.}}

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj|scheißen<schiss,geschissen>}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|vulgar|to shit}} {{l|de|kacken}}, {{l|de|koten}}, {{l|de|Stuhlgang haben}}
* {{sense|vulgar|to be uninterested}} {{l|de|pfeifen}}

